From 719c7a67bd639143157d6d71d4709b056fc1413a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 23:40:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 042/114] rust: usb: add topology lookup and removal
 notification

Expose an owned root-first bus/port path for a USB device and a safe
synchronous lookup which returns a reference-counted matching device.

Add an RAII wrapper around the USB notifier chain for drivers which
associate separately-created devices with a USB topology node. The
callback receives a borrowed typed device and unregistration is tied
to the pinned notifier owner.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
